 destroyed the phone stating quote i  remember ripping the phone off the wall  depp also admitted that he had  previously taken responsibility for  severing his finger though depp claimed  that he was only trying to protect herd  when he had to tell the production  company the injury prevented him from  working on set and depp also confirmed  that he wrote messages  for heard in blood paint and lipstick  including quote i love you and good luck  which he did to indicate he felt the  relationship was over  and in a trial that had the couple  airing out their dirty laundry depp also  detailed an alleged incident involving  literal dirty laundry supposedly on the  night of herd's birthday party in april  2016 depp says he arrived late due to a  meeting he was attending that testified  that heard was furious with him hitting  him multiple times after the party ended  before he left and spent the night at  another home depp said that he planned  to retrieve items the next morning after  heard left for coachella but was told by  someone at the home who texted him a  photo not to return because  there was poop in the bed quote it was a  photograph of the bed our bed and on my  side of the bed was human fecal matter  so i understood why it wasn't a good  time to go down there  he continued my initial response to that  was i mean i laughed it was so outside  it was so bizarre and so grotesque that  i could only laugh depp had previously  claimed in a written statement that  heard or one of her friends were the  culprit and allege that heard had called  this quote just a harmless prank but  depp said that incident was when he knew  their marriage was over and a month  later heard filed for divorce  hurd has denied any role in this poo  donet suggesting the story is fabricated  simply to  humiliate her so yeah the british trial  was incredibly colorful  and after hearing all the evidence the  uk court sided with the sun and rejected  depp's libel claims in his november 2020  opinion justice andrew nichol concluded  that the sun had met its burden of proof  and that the sun's allegations that depp  engaged in unprovoked attacks and  violent conduct against his then wife  that caused her to be in fear for her  life were true quote on the balance of  the probabilities meaning the abuse  allegations were more likely than not to  be true the justice did not accept  depp's characterization of heard as a  gold digger who had quote constructed a  hoax and as an insurance policy in the  event the marriage fell apart among the  incidents the judge found to be  substantially true were the two events  alluded to in herd's 2016 application  for domestic violence restraining order  the may 2016 assault with depp's phone  and the severe december 2015 incident  where depp allegedly threw a decanter at  heard in the penthouse head-butted her  and pulled large chunks of hair from her  scalp before an appearance on james  corden's late late show and the justice  did not find depp's claim that hurd was  responsible for severing his fingertip  to be credible and as for the poop in  the bed incident while the judge blamed  the dog  for what it's worth i consider it  unlikely that miss heard or one of her  friends was responsible reasoning in  part that depp was out of the house at  the time of the incident and heard was  the one likely to suffer from  the effects the judge concluded quote it  was therefore a singularly ineffective  means for miss heard or one of her  friends to get back at mr depp your  mileage may vary on that reasoning in  response to the ruling depths  representative stated they found the  decision quote as perverse as it is  bewildering and immediately announced  their intention to appeal but in march  of 2021 depp's appeal was rejected and  the court of appeals ruled that the  lower court case was quote full and fair  and the trial judge conclusions quote  have not been shown to even arguably be  vitiated by any error or approach of  mistake of law and concluded the appeal  has no real prospect of success and that  there is no other compelling reason for  it to be heard on appeal depp's council  had argued they did not get a fair  hearing and that hurt was an unreliable  witness and as evidence of her  unreliability depp's counsel asserted  that herd has not kept her promise to  donate her 7 million divorce settlement  to charity and the fallout from depp's  spectacular defeat was immediate  following the november ruling depp  announced he was leaving the fantastic  beasts franchise after warner brother  requested his resignation and that takes  us to the good old us of a because what  makes depp's defeat so notable is that  the odds of prevailing on a libel claim  are much higher in england than in the  us in england the party accused of  defamation has the burden of proving  that their claim is quote substantially  true now that's the opposite in the u.s  where the defamed person has the burden  of proving that the libel of statements  are false  another reason us defamation cases are  hard to win is that public figures like  depp must prove the defamatory  statements were made with actual mouse  meaning that they were published with  knowledge of being false or reckless  disregard for their truth or falsity  again actual malice has nothing to do  with not liking a person it is an  evidentiary standard uh and it's not  particularly well named it's a legal  term of art and even with these built-in  advantages depp's still lost twice in  the uk  in the face of double defeat some have  characterized dep's legal strategy as a  complete flop and remember not only have  two british courts found herd's abuse  allegations to be substantially true but  depp's efforts have had the unintended  streizan effect of amplifying these  allegations after all if not for depp's  multiple lawsuits there would be no  reason for this channel to make a video  on this controversy to the millions of  legal eagles subscribers it's a case of  life imitating art i guess but depp's  defenders insist that the british trial  was not fairly decided that new evidence  has since come forward that paints a  different picture particularly with new  audio that purports to show her  admitting to abusing depp  so after all of this we find ourselves  back on american soil as depp attempts  another bite of the defamation apple  hoping this time he will be vindicated  and particularly an issue in the  american trial is an op-ed that amber  heard published on december 18 2018 six  months after depp filed the uk libel  action where she published in the  washington post  an article entitled i spoke up against  sexual violence and faced our culture's  wrath that has to change heard wrote  like many women i had been harassed and  sexually assaulted by the time i was of  college age but i kept quiet i did not  expect filing complaints to bring  justice and i didn't see myself as a  victim then two years ago i became a  public figure representing domestic  abuse and i felt the full force of our  culture's wrath for women who speak out  and in march 2019 depp responded to the  op-ed by filing a 50 million defamation  lawsuit against his ex-wife contending  heard's article contained quote  categorically and demonstrably false  claims of domestic abuse  the op-ed depended on the central  premise that ms heard was a domestic  abuse victim and that mr depp  perpetrated domestic violence against  her depp's lawyers also wrote in the  complaint quote her allegations are part  of an elaborate hoax to generate  positive publicity for miss heard and  advance her career the complaint which  again are just allegations from one side  charged that heard had incalculably  damaged the actor's reputation and  derailed his career highlighting that  disney fired debt from the pirates of  the caribbean franchise four days after  the publication of herd's article  and though the article does not mention  depth by name a party 